  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health Information Systems</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fragmented care delivery, increase of chronic illnesses, lack of ICT-based information systems and inefficiencies in existing referral systems put exponential pressure on resources of hospitals in African countries and leads to unequal distribution of access to healthcare as well as unnecessary revenue losses. Implementing Health Information Systems (eHIS) has the potential to strongly improve access to healthcare and improve (cash) management of health facilities. Africa eHealth Solutions International B.V. is an impact driven Dutch company that searches to contribute to the development of the African health sector. Its mission is to create affordable quality care for all. To introduce and scale-up data driven e-health services in African countries, Technical Assistance (DGGF-TA) provided support to pilot and scale-up the implementation of the systems into hospitals. At the moment, there are 9 hospitals up and running. During this project 25 direct FTE were supported, 360 people trained within hospitals, as well as by community outreach.</narrative>
  </description>
